H1315G.def:
A woman of the tribe of Judah living at the time of United Monarchy, only mentioned at 1 Rois 4:15; 
daughter of: Solomon (H8010); 
sister of: Taphath (H2955) and Rehoboam (H7346); married to Ahimaaz (H0290I)
§ Bashemath or Basmath = "spice"
1) Hittite wife of Esau, daughter of Ishmael, sister of Nebaioth
2) daughter of Solomon, wife of Ahimaaz, one of Solomon's commissariat officers

H1315H.def:
A woman living at the time before the Flood, first mentioned at Genèse 26:34; 
daughter of: Elon (H0356); married to Esau (H6215); 
mother of: Eliphaz (H0464); also called Basemath (KJV: Bashemath) at Genèse 26:34; 
Another name of a.dah (עָדָה "Adah" H5711H)
§ Bashemath or Basmath = "spice"
1) Hittite wife of Esau, daughter of Ishmael, sister of Nebaioth
2) daughter of Solomon, wife of Ahimaaz, one of Solomon's commissariat officers

H1315I.def:
A woman of the Arabs living at the time of the Patriarchs, first mentioned at Genèse 28:9; 
daughter of: Ishmael (H3458); 
sister of: Nebaioth (H5032), Kedar (H6938), Adbeel (H0110), Mibsam (H4017), Mishma (H4927), Dumah (H1746), Massa (H4854), Hadad (H2301), Tema (H8485), Jetur (H3195), Naphish (H5305) and Kedemah (H6929); married to Esau (H6215); 
mother of: Reuel (H7467); also called Basemath (KJV: Bashemath) at Genèse 36:3,4,10,13,17; 
Another name of ma.cha.lat (מַחֲלַת "Mahalath" H4258G)
§ Bashemath or Basmath = "spice"
1) Hittite wife of Esau, daughter of Ishmael, sister of Nebaioth
2) daughter of Solomon, wife of Ahimaaz, one of Solomon's commissariat officers

H1323I.def:
A woman living at the time of the Patriarchs, first mentioned at Genèse 38:2; 
daughter of: Shua (H7770); married to Judah (H3063); 
mother of: Er (H6147), Onan (H0209) and Shelah (H7956)
the wife of Uriah whom David had murdered, having had adulterous relations with her; subsequently wife of David and mother of Solomon, Shimea, Shobab, and Nathan (alternate spelling to 'Bathsheba')

H1328A.def:
A man living at the time of the Patriarchs, first mentioned at Genèse 22:22; 
son of: Nahor (H5152H) and Milcah (H4435); 
brother of: Uz (H5780H), Buz (H0938), Kemuel (H7055), Chesed (H3777), Hazo (H2375), Pildash (H6394), Jidlaph (H3044) and Tebah (H2875); 
half-brother of: Gaham (H1514), Tahash (H8477) and Maacah (H4601); 
father of: Rebekah (H7259) and Laban (H3837A)
§ Bethuel = "God destroys" or "man of God" or "dweller in God"
nephew of Abraham, son of Nahor by Milcah, father of Rebekah

H1332.def:
A woman of the Egyptians living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1 Chroniques 4:18; 
daughter of: Pharaoh (H6547M); married to Mered (H4778)(?); 
mother of: Miriam (H4813H), Shammai (H8060I) and Ishbah (H3431) 
§ Bithiah = "daughter of Jehovah"
a daughter of a Pharaoh and wife of Mered of Judah

H1339.def:
A woman living at the time of United Monarchy, first mentioned at 2 Samuel 11:3; 
daughter of: Eliam (H0463); married to David (H1732) and Uriah (H0223A); 
mother of: Shammua (H8051H), Shobab (H7727), Nathan (H5416) and Solomon (H8010); also called Bath-shua at 1 Chroniques 3:5; 
Also named: bat-shu.a (בַּת־שׁוּעַ "Bath-shua" H1340) 
§ Bath-sheba = "daughter of an oath"
the wife of Uriah whom David had murdered, having had adulterous relations with her; subsequently wife of David and mother of Solomon, Shimea, Shobab, and Nathan

H1340.def:
A woman living at the time of United Monarchy, first mentioned at 2 Samuel 11:3; 
daughter of: Eliam (H0463); married to David (H1732) and Uriah (H0223A); 
mother of: Shammua (H8051H), Shobab (H7727), Nathan (H5416) and Solomon (H8010); also called Bath-shua at 1 Chroniques 3:5; 
Another spelling of bat-she.va (בַּת־שֶׁ֫בַע "Bathsheba" H1339) 
§ Bath-shua = "daughter of wealth"
1) the wife of Uriah whom David had murdered, having had adulterous relations with her; subsequently wife of David and mother of Solomon, Shimea, Shobab, and Nathan (alternate spelling to 'Bathsheba')
2) wife of Judah

H1373.def:
A man living at the time of Exile and Return, only mentioned at Néhémie 11:8; also translated "men"; 
§ Gabbai = "my back"
the head of an important Benjamite family living in Jerusalem in the time of Nehemiah

H1388.def:
A man of the tribe of Judah living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1 Chroniques 2:49; 
son of: Sheva (H7724); 
brother of: Machbenah (H4343) 
§ Gibea = "hill"
son of Sheva and grandson of Caleb (a son of Caleb)
